  "independentDerivations": [
    "Spherical symmetry makes exterior E radial and constant on each concentric sphere. Flux through area4*pi*r^2 gives |q|/(4*pi*epsilon0*epsilon*r^2). The conductor interior is zero in static equilibrium; exterior normal field may jump at the charged surface.",
    "A sheet pillbox has two equal outgoing flux magnitudes E*A, totaling2*E*A=sigma*A/(epsilon0*epsilon). For a conductor surface the interior contribution is zero, leaving one exterior flux term; the factor differs for the same free surface density.",
    "Force/charge has SI unit N/C. Sigma divided by permittivity gives that unit only when sigma uses C/m^2. The absolute values in preserved sphere/sheet formulas compute magnitude, while sign controls radial/normal direction."
  ],
